     Try running a Valkrie (I can never spell that character class right).
When you reach character level 5, dip your longsword in a fountain.  In
general, one or two dips turns it into an Excalibur, especially if your
luck is good.  Excalibur is +5 to hit and +10 damage, does not allow the
monster in question to regenerate any hit points lost, is listed as "defender"
whose meaning I don't know, and also gives you automatic searching.  Neat
toy.  Doesn't have poison resistance automatically (you can get it from a
gelatinous cube corpse), but does have cold resistance and gets speed at
level 7 (I believe a Barbarian does as well).

:FIVE, count 'em FIVE pages of stuff.  AND ALL OF IT CURSED!   WAAAAAAAA!
:And me without my Neutral altar handy.  Shucks.  What's the best way
:to tackle this pile (I've saved the game)
     You'll need holy water.  Don't try polymorphing it-- objects will
retain their curses.  Pick out what you want and dip it in the holy water--
there's really no other way.
     Wait, there is a way.  Obtain a blessed scroll of remove curse.  Drop
all your inventory (except the scroll).  (You can also just get an ordinary
scroll and dip it in holy water, or you can simply use an ordinary scroll,
but it only works on what you're wearing and wielding, so it'll have limited
impact.)  Pick up all the useful objects you can carry.  Read the scroll.
All of them will become uncursed.

